WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.507 --> 00:00:03.861
(humming My Girl by The Temptations)

00:00:03.861 --> 00:00:08.861
♪ I've got sunshine on a cloudy day. ♪

00:00:13.302 --> 00:00:17.049
♪ When it's cold outside ♪

00:00:17.049 --> 00:00:21.270
♪ I've got the month of May. ♪

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:23.220
- If you've ever ranked
yourself against others

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:24.840
based on a specific trait,

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:26.940
what would it say about how you see them

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:28.443
and how they see you?

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:31.200
We brought together five singers

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:32.610
and had them rank themselves

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:35.370
based on their perceived singing talent.

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:38.403
Then we rearranged them based
on our audiences' votes.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:40.833
This is Ranking.

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:45.330
- Hi my name is Layla. I am 19 years old

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:48.510
and I am a singer-songwriter
for about like, 5+ years.

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:50.760
And I'm from Redlands, California.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:54.810
- Hi, my name is Edmond. I am
from Chino Hills, California.

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:56.850
I am not a professional singer.

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:59.580
I just do it for fun in
the car or in karaoke.

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:02.730
- I'm Richard. I am
from Colombus, Georgia.

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:05.580
And I make music under
the name SimplyRich.

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:07.440
I am a singer, rapper, and producer.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:09.900
By day I am a software engineer.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:13.230
- Hello, I'm Danny. My
pronouns are they/them.

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:15.930
I am 33 years old and
I've been singing since

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:18.153
I was, I don't know- fresh out the womb.

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:23.220
- Hello, I am Oksanna. The
passion, the dream has always

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:27.270
been since I was a young kid,
to be like Hannah Montana.

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:29.340
But I'm trying to figure
out what that looks like now

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:31.803
as an adult under the name Osie.

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:39.733
♪ Most days I'm fine but
when I'm not I'm falling ♪

00:01:39.733 --> 00:01:43.366
♪ in deep into the clutch of ♪

00:01:43.366 --> 00:01:47.421
♪ those regrets of what
I was supposed to do. ♪

00:01:47.421 --> 00:01:52.421
♪ What I was supposed to do. ♪

00:01:54.681 --> 00:01:58.890
♪ So wake me up when it's all over. ♪

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:02.590
♪ When I'm wiser and I'm older. ♪

00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:07.590
♪ All this time I was
finding myself and I ♪

00:02:08.164 --> 00:02:13.164
♪ didn't know I was lost. ♪

00:02:13.359 --> 00:02:17.075
♪ I'm getting closer and closer ♪

00:02:17.075 --> 00:02:20.499
♪ to get you off my brain. ♪

00:02:20.499 --> 00:02:24.073
♪ Closure is supposed to ♪

00:02:24.073 --> 00:02:27.957
♪ feel this way because
I wanna call it quits ♪

00:02:27.957 --> 00:02:32.957
♪ and brought us to our end. ♪

00:02:33.058 --> 00:02:37.291
♪ Girl I know this might seem strange, ♪

00:02:37.291 --> 00:02:40.640
♪ I just gotta let you know 'cause ♪

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:42.983
♪ 'cause I'm feeling this way. ♪

00:02:42.983 --> 00:02:47.689
♪ See I've been watching
you for a while. ♪

00:02:47.689 --> 00:02:50.230
♪ Tired of being a stranger. ♪

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:55.230
♪ Why would you even try? ♪

00:02:55.637 --> 00:02:58.948
♪ Can we stay together
and I mean forever. ♪

00:02:58.948 --> 00:03:03.548
♪ You changed me for the better. ♪

00:03:03.548 --> 00:03:08.465
♪ And I know, I know,
I know you got this. ♪

00:03:09.641 --> 00:03:11.891
(clapping)

00:03:16.066 --> 00:03:17.223
- [Layla] It's gonna be hard.

00:03:17.223 --> 00:03:18.690
- [Oksanna] What might be an easier way

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:20.880
to say so it's not like, "oh
you're the least talented."

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:23.730
More like, maybe experience?
Might be an easier-

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:25.740
- [Danny] Well I'm the oldest. So, what?

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:27.018
- [Oksanna] True.

00:03:27.018 --> 00:03:28.140
- By a lot so.

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:30.600
- I have no professional
experience in this so I will

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:33.450
work my way down. That is
totally fine, I'm okay with it.

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:36.707
- [Danny] I'll go here.

00:03:36.707 --> 00:03:40.470
- I feel like with music there is like,

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:42.690
kind of an objective way
to kind of like, rank.

00:03:42.690 --> 00:03:43.980
But there is also like,

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:46.703
a more subjective way of how
does this thing make you feel?

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:50.250
So which one do we want
to like, go off of?

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:51.990
- I felt things with you.

00:03:51.990 --> 00:03:52.953
- Exactly. Yup.

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:56.940
- So I think you and I should switch.

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:58.323
'Cause I feel like, yes.

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:03.360
- [Oksanna] Does technique and
knowing that kind of stuff-

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:07.260
Do you feel like that adds to
being on your level of skills?

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:10.080
Knowing how to do runs or
knowing like, harmonies.

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:11.649
Things like that?

00:04:11.649 --> 00:04:13.800
- I feel like yeah, because
it is ranking singers

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:16.290
and not artists or singer-songwriters.

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:17.123
- [Oksanna] True.

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:18.510
- I definitely think a great singer

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:19.890
really evokes that emotion

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:22.961
and makes you feel something.
So despite technique, like,

00:04:22.961 --> 00:04:25.410
just like, really having that-
something that resonates.

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:26.731
I think that is really important.

00:04:26.731 --> 00:04:27.564
(group agrees)

00:04:27.564 --> 00:04:29.190
- [Layla] Maybe base it off that.

00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:32.160
- I mean, in high school I
was in choir, musical theater.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:34.260
You feel it. Like, oh high school choir.

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:35.910
Same? Were you a tenor?

00:04:35.910 --> 00:04:36.743
- Choir, acapella.

00:04:36.743 --> 00:04:38.850
I sang tenor and bass
depending on what was needed.

00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:41.820
- [Danny] Tenor and bass? Range!

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:43.620
So you're going to stay right there.

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:47.460
Effortless. That's my big thing.

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:49.020
The ability to harmonize.

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:51.690
- [Layla] Yes. That's a
skill within itself, yeah.

00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:56.310
- I might regret this, but
do we wanna try harmonizing?

00:04:56.310 --> 00:04:58.160
- I was just thinking the same thing.

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:00.780
Okay so what do we
wanna- like just a note?

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:02.130
- Like, "My Girl" or something?

00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:03.540
- Yes! Oh my gosh.

00:05:04.972 --> 00:05:07.691
(harmonizing My Girl by The Temptations)

00:05:07.691 --> 00:05:11.157
♪ I've got sunshine ♪

00:05:11.157 --> 00:05:16.157
♪ on a cloudy day. ♪

00:05:16.498 --> 00:05:20.547
♪ When it's cold outside ♪

00:05:20.547 --> 00:05:25.027
♪ I've got the month of May. ♪

00:05:25.027 --> 00:05:29.485
♪ Well I guess you'd say, ♪

00:05:29.485 --> 00:05:34.290
♪ what can make me feel this way? ♪

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:35.123
♪ My girl. ♪

00:05:35.123 --> 00:05:35.956
♪ My girl. ♪

00:05:35.956 --> 00:05:38.015
♪ My girl. ♪

00:05:38.015 --> 00:05:40.790
♪ Talking about my girl. ♪

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:42.426
♪ My girl. ♪

00:05:42.426 --> 00:05:44.104
(cheering)

00:05:44.104 --> 00:05:46.803
- [Edmond] We just started a band!

00:05:46.803 --> 00:05:48.390
- Well we sound really good together

00:05:48.390 --> 00:05:50.582
but we're supposed to rank each other.

00:05:50.582 --> 00:05:51.415
- [Layla] Okay. Okay.

00:05:51.415 --> 00:05:54.420
- I mean, I'm okay with
the level I sing at.

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:55.590
But compared to you guys,

00:05:55.590 --> 00:05:57.690
you got more experience and
can actually play instruments

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:59.640
and pursue it semi-professionally.

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:02.460
- I mean, it's hard to say
because in a similar way

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:03.990
I started singing when I was very young.

00:06:03.990 --> 00:06:07.260
But singing well, that
didn't come till later.

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:09.990
Like the voice lessons, how
to play more instruments,

00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:12.330
and learning how to just
be with other musicians.

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:14.880
- I wanna be like Prince and
play at least 28 instruments.

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:16.260
Right? That would be cool?

00:06:16.260 --> 00:06:18.990
- You can hear the
musicality in your voice.

00:06:18.990 --> 00:06:19.860
- Can you? Oh, I appreciate that.

00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:23.010
- After college I was kinda
like, existential crisis

00:06:23.010 --> 00:06:25.080
a little bit because I didn't
know what I wanted to do.

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:27.012
I know I wanted to not be broke.

00:06:27.012 --> 00:06:28.190
(laughing)

00:06:28.190 --> 00:06:29.023
- [Richard] So I focused
on software engineering.

00:06:29.023 --> 00:06:31.080
My sister convinced me to
start making my own music

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:33.600
and it's been like, healing alongside like

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:34.980
journaling and therapy.

00:06:34.980 --> 00:06:36.540
- [Danny] Music for mental health.

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:38.820
- Same thing actually. All
of my songs are kind of all

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:40.760
around mental health stuff
so I'm with you on that.

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:42.720
- Is anyone not content
with what they put forward

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:43.650
and wanna sing?

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:46.520
- I kinda wanna show
like a different side.

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:51.520
♪ I don't wanna wait for
our lives to be over. ♪

00:06:51.681 --> 00:06:53.589
♪ I want to know right now ♪

00:06:53.589 --> 00:06:55.560
♪ what will it be? ♪

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:56.550
- [Layla] Yes!

00:06:56.550 --> 00:06:57.944
- [Oksanna] So gentle.

00:06:57.944 --> 00:06:59.232
(clapping)

00:06:59.232 --> 00:07:01.170
- It's when you get to
the vowels, like that "e".

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:02.850
It just becomes just very angelic.

00:07:02.850 --> 00:07:06.723
- Okay, humble brag but I
have heard angelic before.

00:07:06.723 --> 00:07:07.556
(laughing)

00:07:07.556 --> 00:07:08.389
- He's like, not to brag-

00:07:08.389 --> 00:07:10.500
- [Oksanna] Well for good reason then.

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:13.140
- Okay, are we content- is
anyone unhappy with their spot?

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:15.993
- I mean, I'm competitive
so I wanna be the first but-

00:07:16.952 --> 00:07:19.800
- I mean he sang a second thing.
I can sing a second thing.

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:20.965
- Yeah, let's hear it. Let's hear it.

00:07:20.965 --> 00:07:22.662
- [Richard] Okay.

00:07:22.662 --> 00:07:26.829
♪ Hey, can I go, wanna go deeper. ♪

00:07:30.057 --> 00:07:31.557
- You better stay right there.

00:07:32.442 --> 00:07:34.337
- Soul Train, yeah.

00:07:34.337 --> 00:07:35.798
- How do we feel?

00:07:35.798 --> 00:07:39.448
- I feel content because genuinely like,

00:07:39.448 --> 00:07:40.950
you guys are great

00:07:40.950 --> 00:07:42.270
and you guys are also great.

00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:45.630
I feel like emotion is just, yeah.

00:07:45.630 --> 00:07:48.870
I think we can all agree
that we really felt that too.

00:07:48.870 --> 00:07:49.703
- We did.

00:07:52.699 --> 00:07:55.366
(hip hop music)

00:07:56.930 --> 00:07:58.530
- [Male Voice] First
off, Layla I'll have you

00:07:58.530 --> 00:08:00.163
switch with Ed.

00:08:05.401 --> 00:08:07.133
Ed I'll have you switch with Oksanna.

00:08:10.950 --> 00:08:12.867
- [Danny] Now I'm nervous.

00:08:12.867 --> 00:08:14.273
- [Male Voice] Oksanna I'll
have you switch with Danny.

00:08:18.031 --> 00:08:20.179
And then last but not least,
Oksanna I'll have you switch

00:08:20.179 --> 00:08:22.990
one more time with Richard.

00:08:22.990 --> 00:08:24.510
- [Oksanna] What?

00:08:24.510 --> 00:08:27.270
- [Male Voice] And these
are the audience results.

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:29.670
- I feel like the emoji
that- (explosion sound).

00:08:32.640 --> 00:08:36.150
I did not expect that at
all because I do believe

00:08:36.150 --> 00:08:37.680
that there is always something

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:39.270
where you can learn as an artist.

00:08:39.270 --> 00:08:41.370
And I know I still have
a long way to grow.

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:43.830
- I like how everyone
brought our unique sound

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:45.750
and tone and style and everything.

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:48.210
- I'm surprised about-

00:08:48.210 --> 00:08:50.370
- I can't lie, I'm also surprised.

00:08:50.370 --> 00:08:52.020
- I don't know maybe it
was her song choices.

00:08:52.020 --> 00:08:53.760
I was just a big fan of her voice.

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:56.160
- I guess I need more variety and range.

00:08:56.160 --> 00:08:58.680
I wish I would've came
out and showed that more.

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:01.140
But I think that's the
beautiful thing about music.

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:03.420
It's that art is so subjective
and sometimes it doesn't

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:05.250
always resonate with anyone and like,

00:09:05.250 --> 00:09:06.450
that's the beauty of it.

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:10.180
- As long as Richard's ahead of me like,

00:09:11.253 --> 00:09:12.974
then things are correct.

00:09:12.974 --> 00:09:14.880
- I never would have put
the ranking this way but

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:16.530
honored that it went that way.

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:19.547
- The purity though, the purity.

00:09:19.547 --> 00:09:23.100
- Out of all five of us, she
was the most original sound.

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:25.350
It's like, oh, it's something new.

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:26.183
- Fresh.

00:09:26.183 --> 00:09:27.390
- [Danny] It felt fresh.

00:09:27.390 --> 00:09:30.090
It was so fun to sing together.

00:09:30.090 --> 00:09:31.980
- [Edmond] Let's all go for karaoke.

00:09:31.980 --> 00:09:35.222
- That choir thing will
always be one of the coolest

00:09:35.222 --> 00:09:36.330
moments I've gotten to
experience in a long time.

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:37.793
- [Edmond] It's like the wave.

00:09:38.940 --> 00:09:41.370
- [Danny] Well, let's do a wave.

00:09:41.370 --> 00:09:43.920
You said wave, let's do a wave.

00:09:43.920 --> 00:09:44.753
- [Edmond] Am I starting?

00:09:44.753 --> 00:09:46.141
- [Danny] Yeah, you start.

00:09:46.141 --> 00:09:48.391
(cheering)

